21. Canonical Doctrine
Do not only remember what was learned. Remember how it became learnable. Do not merely search the map; search for representations, operators, and search rules that change what the map can contain. Preserve invariants, measure deltas, validate reality, compress successful machinery into callable Seals, and let experience improve the machinery that produces the next experience.

